# /research/ was renamed to /projects/ (2026-07-30). These rules keep every
# old URL alive, which matters for more than bookmarks: App Store builds
# already in the wild fetch /research/projects/<folder>/index.md. URLSession
# follows 301s, so those installs keep working until the next release ships.
#
# The technology.json and technology/ rules were dropped 2026-07-30 with the toy catalog itself.
# The shipped App Store build's Research tab fetches that file and will show an
# error until a new build ships — the replacement gallery tab needs no such
# file.
#
# Project folders also lost a path segment in the move
# (/research/projects/X/ → /projects/X/), so that prefix needs its own rule
# that collapses the extra segment.
#
# ⚠️ Every source pattern here is DISJOINT on purpose. A catch-all
# `/research/* → /projects/:splat` alongside the more specific
# `/research/projects/*` rule looked correct and was not: Workers Static
# Assets did not honour first-match-wins by file order, the catch-all won,
# and /research/projects/X/ resolved to /projects/projects/X/ (404). Do not
# reintroduce an overlapping catch-all — enumerate instead.
#
# THE SECOND RENAME (2026-08-01): gallery → thewall. The wall's manifest and
# its picture folder were renamed to match the name the thing has always had in
# prose. Shipped App Store builds hardcode /projects/gallery.json in
# APIClient.swift, so that URL has to keep answering — and because the manifest
# it now redirects to points its tiles at /projects/thewall/..., the picture
# folder needs its own rule for anything holding an older copy of the JSON.
# The /research/gallery.json rule below points straight at the new name rather
# than chaining through the old one — one hop, not two.
#
# Served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets, which reads this file from the
# assets directory. The Worker itself is still a pure passthrough.

/research/projects/*     /projects/:splat             301
/research/gallery.json   /projects/thewall.json       301
/research/               /projects/                   301
/research                 /projects                   301

/projects/gallery.json   /projects/thewall.json       301
/projects/gallery/*      /projects/thewall/:splat     301
